doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:29:3. The name of the author may not be used to endorse or promote products
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:58:	<li>RAM: Up to 256 MB works well, up to 1 GB (max of what a real O2 can handle) works with OpenBSD/sgi (and possibly the raw PROM)
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:61:	<li>On-board O2 graphics; works well enough to run NetBSD/sgimips with X11.
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:63:	<li>Ethernet, enough to (barely) run OpenBSD and NetBSD with root-on-nfs.
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:71:	<li><a href="#netbsdsgimips">NetBSD/sgimips</a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:72:	<li><a href="#openbsdsgiinstall">OpenBSD/sgi</a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:73:	<li><small><a href="#linuxforo2"><font color="red">Linux for O2</font></a> (not yet)</small>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:74:	<li><small><a href="#IRIX"><font color="red">IRIX</font></a> (not yet)</small>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:77:<p>and also some hints on how to make a <a href="#prom">backup copy of the PROM</a> from your own O2 and run it in the emulator.
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:83:<a name="netbsdsgimips"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:84:<h3>NetBSD/sgimips:</h3>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:87:<a href="20060623-netbsd-sgimips-3.0.png"><img src="20060623-netbsd-sgimips-3.0_small.png"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:88:<a href="20190612-netbsd-sgimips-1.png"><img src="20190612-netbsd-sgimips-1_small.png"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:89:<a href="20190612-netbsd-sgimips-2.png"><img src="20190612-netbsd-sgimips-2_small.png"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:91:<p><a href="http://www.netbsd.org/ports/sgimips/">NetBSD/sgimips</a> can run
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:92:in GXemul on an emulated SGI O2 (also known as IP32). The SCSI controller
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:93:is not emulated yet, so NetBSD needs to boot with root-on-NFS:
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:99:	<a href="machine_decstation.html#netbsdpmaxinstall">Install NetBSD/pmax 8.0 from CDROM</a>.
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:105:  <li>Download the files corresponding to a NetBSD/sgimips CD-ROM iso image, and the
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:107:	<a href="ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0/sgimips/binary/kernel/netbsd-GENERIC32_IP3x.gz">ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0/sgimips/binary/kernel/netbsd-GENERIC32_IP3x.gz</a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:108:	<a href="ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0/sgimips/binary/kernel/netbsd-INSTALL32_IP3x.gz">ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0/sgimips/binary/kernel/netbsd-INSTALL32_IP3x.gz</a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:110:	wget -np -l 0 -r <a href="ftp://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0/sgimips/binary/sets/">ftp://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0/sgimips/binary/sets/</a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:111:	mkisofs -U -o sgimips.iso ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-8.0
