doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:444:<a name="IRIX"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:445:<h3>Experimenting with booting IRIX from a real SGI O2</h3>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:456:<p>where <tt>unix</tt> is the IP32 kernel. If you do not want to use
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:461:<a href="20190526-irix-not-really-working-yet.png"><img src="20190526-irix-not-really-working-yet_small.png"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:464:IRIX Release 6.5 IP32 Version 10151453 System V
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:487:most importantly there is no way to get IRIX to find the root file system
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:489:GXemul is not good enough for IRIX to accept it for root-on-nfs. Also,
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:498:<a name="prom"></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:499:<h3>Experimenting with a PROM from a real SGI O2</h3>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:501:<p>Note: Normally, a dump of the PROM image from your real SGI O2 is <i>not</i> needed,
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:504:<p>Using a serial console hooked up to your O2, executing the PROM command
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:510:will dump 512 KB of the PROM range. Make sure you capture all the output
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:513:the GXemul source code distribution: <tt>experiments/sgiprom_to_bin</tt>.)
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:515:<p>Assuming you have extracted the PROM from your real machine into a
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:516:file called <tt>prom</tt>, the following example shows how to start up the
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:520:$ <b>gxemul -Q -X -e o2 0xbfc00000:prom</b>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:523:<p><tt>-Q</tt> turns off GXemul's built-in PROM emulation, allowing raw PROM images
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:531: <a href="20180910-sgiip32prom-4.13.png"><img src="20180910-sgiip32prom-4.13.png" width=250></a>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:537:NOTE: The SGI O2 PROM does some hardware tests during startup that do not
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:540:This has been verified to work with PROM versions 2.3, 4.13, and 4.18.
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:543:<p>With a IP32 PROM version 4.13 for example, if the hack is commented out,
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:547:$ <b>gxemul -p 0xffffffffbfc05180 -X -Q -e o2 0xbfc00000:prom-4.13</b>
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:556:<p>If the 'console' variable in the PROM's environment variable section
doc/machine_sgi_o2.html:565:NetBSD, OpenBSD, and perhaps also Linux, other things may not work.
