  362: /*
  363:  * On the VMEbus, only one cpu may be configured to respond to any
  364:  * particular vme ipl. Therefore, it wouldn't make sense to globally
  365:  * enable all the interrupts all the time -- it would not be possible
  366:  * to put two cpu's and one vme card into a single cage. Rather, we
  367:  * enable each vme interrupt only when we are attaching a device that
  368:  * uses it. This makes it easier (though not trivial) to put two cpu
  369:  * cards in one VME cage, and both can have some limited access to vme
  370:  * interrupts (just can't share the same irq).
  439: /*
  440:  * XXX what AM bits should be used for the D32/D16 mappings?
