codex
There is a wider-callback case too: IP32’s MEC model makes 32-byte descriptor reads through `memory_rw`, so the scalar CPU width limit is not a global callback limit.

The compatibility question also has a useful bound: a successful pre-fix run cannot have traversed either unconditional `exit(1)` arm. The review must preserve existing supported accesses and assess the newly surviving refusal behavior separately.
